CONCLUSION - Negative-Index Retrieval in Paired-Nanorod Metamaterials
==============================================================================

SIGN CONVENTION (stated explicitly): time dependence e^{-i omega t}; the slab
forward model is t = 4 z e^{i beta} / [(1+z)^2 - (1-z)^2 e^{2 i beta}],
r = (1-z^2)(1-e^{2 i beta}) / [(1+z)^2 - (1-z)^2 e^{2 i beta}], beta = 2 pi n d / lambda.
With this convention a passive (absorbing) medium has Im(n) > 0 and Re(z) > 0,
and the passive retrieval root is |u| <= 1 for u = e^{i beta} = e^{i 2 pi n d/lambda}.
All reported n_imag / z_imag values follow this convention.
The calibration data reconstruct from retrieved (n, z) to a max RMSE of 2.6e-16, confirming the exact effective-slab model manifold.

WORKFLOW: (1) phase-aware retrieval of n, z from measured |t|, |r| and unwrapped
phases on the provided 126-point grid; (2) per-sample fits of three compact
Lorentz-resonance families; (3) LOOCV-validated linear geometry->parameter
transfer maps tied to the family parameters; (4) held-out spectra generated ONLY
by the selected family + its transfer map (no interpolation or surrogate APIs);
(5) negative-index summary from n_real < 0 grid points (first/last rule, with the
documented zero-width no-band fallback).

